PERF

This folder keeps performance records for tam-pane: one file per report.
Reports record measured startup timing, memory usage, CPU/GPU overhead,
and relative comparisons against earlier tam-pane builds or other
Wayland compositors (such as Hyprland).

A performance record is observed evidence from a specific build and
measurement method. Keep it unchanged after it is written so later
reports can be compared against it.


NAMING

  PR<nn>-<short-name>.md, for example PR01-hyprland-vs-tam-pane-launch.md.
  Numbers count up from PR01 and are never reused. The date goes inside
  the record.


RECORD TEMPLATE

  Copy this into a new file:

    # PR<nn>: <title>

    - **Date:** YYYY-MM-DD
    - **Builds:** tam-pane <version> (<commit>), plus any baseline
    - **Tool:** command and version used to measure
    - **Source:** boot ID and UTC time window, or benchmark script

    ## Summary

    Two to five lines: what was measured and the main result.

    ## Results

    Tables and key numbers. Include sample sizes (n) and ranges alongside
    medians.

    ## Observations

    What accounts for the difference (launch path, phases, shared costs).

    ## Limits

    Sample size caveats, missing metrics, or conditions that differed.

  Keep personal data, credentials, and raw machine logs out of these
  records. Cite the system journal by boot ID and UTC time window
  instead.


